ved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0131","ق و م","B001","root_001273","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0132","ق و م","B003","root_001273","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0133","ق و م","B004","root_001273","B004","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0134","ق و م","B008","root_001273","B008","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0135","ك ب ر","B007","root_001281","B007","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0136","ك ب ر","B010","root_001281","B010","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0137","ك ذ ب","B001","root_001290","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0138","ك ذ ب","B002","root_001290","B002","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0139","ك ذ ب","B003","root_001290","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0140","ك ر ه","B001","root_001295","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0141","ك ف ر","B001","root_001307","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0142","ك ف ر","B003","root_001307","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0143","ك ل ل","B003","root_001315","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0144","ك و ن","B001","root_001332","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0145","ك و ن","B003","root_001332","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0146","م ق ت","B001","root_001436","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0147","م ق ت","B010",null,null,"review_nonexistent"],["a-s061-0148","م و ل","B001","root_001457","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0149","ن ج و","B001","root_001476","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0150","ن ج و","B003","root_001476","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0151","ن ص ر","B001","root_001510","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0152","ن ص ر","B002","root_001510","B002","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0153","ن ف س","B010","root_001533","B010","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0154","ن ف س","B011","root_001533","B011","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0155","ن ف س","B012","root_001533","B012","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0156","ن ف س","B013","root_001533","B013","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0157","ن ه ر","B001","root_001559","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0158","ن ه ر","B003","root_001559","B003","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0159","ن و ر","B001","root_001564","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0160","ن و ر","B005","root_001564","B005","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0161","ه د ي","B001","root_001583","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0162","ه د ي","B002","root_001583","B002","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s061-0163","ي د ي","B008","root_001693","B008","resolved_source_exact"]],"review_columns":["anchor_key","source_path","line","ayah_ref","raw_excerpt"],"review_rows":[["a-s061-0001","v12/runs/s061/full_context_control/reader_s061_a_ayah_walk.md",25,"61:1","The later surah repeatedly turns apparent abstractions into directed material processes: the path in 61:4 and 61:11, light brought to completion in 61:8, manifestation in 61:9, and rivers running in 61:12. These make B004's coursing image for `سَبَّحَ` more structurally central than it first appeared. The compact building of 61:4 also corrects any reading of `ٱلْعَزِيزُ` as undirected force."],["a-s061-0117","v12/runs/s061/full_context_control/reader_s061_a_ayah_walk.md",33,"61:2","2. **Action as the second speech.** **Lexical evidence:** `ق و ل` B014, “thing's saying as indication,” and `ف ع ل` B001, bringing an act into being. **Structural cue:** `تَقُولُونَ` and `تَفْعَلُونَ` are placed in a balanced positive/negated contrast and repeated in 61:3. **Assigned role:** B014 lets conduct indicate a claim independently of the tongue. **Abductive move:** I infer that when verbal and enacted indications conflict, the absence of action counter-speaks the utterance. **Reading change:** the ayah becomes a clash between two testimonies, not merely between words and silence."],["a-s061-0147","v12/runs/s061/full_context_control/reader_s061_a_ayah_walk.md",43,"61:3","1. **Inconsistency as structural weight.** **Lexical evidence:** `ك ب ر` B010, “greatness as hardship or heaviness,” and `م ق ت` B001, “severe loathing for ugliness.” **Structural cue:** the saying/non-doing construction is repeated verbatim from 61:2, then immediately followed by the tightly joined building of 61:4. **Assigned role:** B010 turns the moral ugliness into a load that a collective structure must bear. **Abductive move:** I infer that repeated unfulfilled speech is one cause of social incohesion, whereas matched action enables compactness. **Reading change:** `كَبُرَ مَقْتًا` reads not only as intensified condemnation but as a warning that inconsistency becomes heavy, deforming material in the community."],["a-s061-0002","v12/runs_11ayah/s061/full_context_control/reader_s061_a_ayah_walk.md",133,"61:7","- The mouth/light image in 61:8 made B008 withholding concrete, while guidance, indication, rescue, and entry in 61:9-61:12 clarified what the call opens toward. The opposed `عَلَى` and `إِلَى` directions therefore became a route-level conflict, not just a rhetorical contrast."]]}
